"First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-x-3.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=-(0)-3=-3,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-(1)-3=-4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=-(2)-3=-5,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-(3)-3=-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-4$ | $-5$ | $-6$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/c9/c96b7da7b073986de68a557df8a9dbde16d39566c87eb0b5ba6ac62bd40da7c4.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-x-3.$\n\n![](images/05/05d10ee3d2e6bc295a7d2e6b07ca726c9c11c159d74f1d81c71fce761fa4275e.png)" 13194139535338 17592186045443 true] [17592186497775 1068 #edb/ref 17592186497771 13194139535338 17592186045443 true] [17592186497775 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535338 17592186045443 true] [17592186497775 1071 "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=2x-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" 13194139535338 17592186045443 true] [17592186497775 1072 #uuid "5da1545d-7bf4-538f-94f3-464d21187a82" 13194139535338 17592186045443 true] [17592186497775 1074 "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=2x-6.$\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=2(0)-6=-6,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=2(1)-6=-4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=2(2)-6=-2,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=2(3)-6=0.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nPlotting these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane: \n\n![](images/95/958c5a848a09e43832324b8afb000348c7630cd2c42e99a51215d48d9895a00e.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of  $y=2x-6.$\n\n![](images/3e/3efb14f33400cd4a6353b93e5d99a826083cca6859785d5bd5d837fb00ad302f.png)" 131941395